From fdf715a05203a1a1f94addd5613601e97121e72e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:46:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rkisp2: Set the DMA segment size

The video nodes import dmabufs through videobuf2-dma-contig, which
requires the mapped scatterlist to be contiguous in the device address
space. The legacy ARM IOMMU DMA operations map an imported buffer in
chunks of the device's maximum segment size, 64 KiB by default, each
with its own IOVA allocation, so a buffer that another queue exported
from the same ISP maps contiguously or not depending on the IOVA
allocation history.

Raise the maximum segment size to the DMA mask so that an imported
buffer is mapped as one contiguous range, as the other Rockchip media
drivers do.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-dev.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-dev.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-dev.c
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-fwnode.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-mc.h>
+#include <media/videobuf2-dma-contig.h>
 
 #include "rkisp2-common.h"
 
@@ -247,6 +248,10 @@ static int rkisp2_probe(struct platform_
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	ret = vb2_dma_contig_set_max_seg_size(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	mutex_init(&rkisp2->stream_lock);
 
 	rkisp2->base_addr = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
